A||||1||Rodrv6||Aluminum Clutch Pedals?||||5||
Z||000000||Rodrv6||04-09-2000||11:58 PM||||I've noticed several references on the forum concerning the problems with the aluminum clutch pedals on some Fieros.  My 84 still has the original aluminum pedal, and after countless clutch pushes over the last 16 years I have never had any trouble with it.  So far it has outlasted 3 clutches.  Are the ones having problems with the pedal bending using heavy duty clutches?  Or have I just been lucky?  I also still have the original clutch master and slave cylinder and have never had any problems with either in over 327,000 miles.  I do change the fluid every two years along with the brakes system fluid, and still have the original brake master cylinder and front calipers with all original seals.  Also just checked and the brake pedal is also aluminum.  I would think that that would cause more trouble than the clutch pedal since the brake is subjected to more foot pressure, but have not heard of anyone having any problems.  Just wondering.||||reg||5
